---
/** Home "method": how each lesson works, as a three-tile bento with drawn art. Copy: docs/v2/copy/home.md#method. */
import Section from './Section.astro';

// OOK: carrier bursts for 1 bits, flat for 0 bits (bits 1 0 1 1 0 1)
const bits = [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1];
const cyc = 6;
const w = 480 / bits.length;
let carrier = '';
bits.forEach((b, i) => {
  const x0 = i * w;
  if (!b) {
    carrier += `M${x0} 60H${x0 + w}`;
    return;
  }
  carrier += `M${x0} 60`;
  for (let k = 0; k < cyc; k++) {
    const x = x0 + (k * w) / cyc;
    const s = w / cyc / 4;
    carrier += `Q${x + s} 34 ${x + 2 * s} 60T${x + 4 * s} 60`;
  }
});
const tile = 'rounded-[1.25rem] border border-border bg-card p-5 sm:p-7';
const k = (t: string) => `<span class="text-scope-peak">${t}</span>`;
const str = (t: string) => `<span class="text-scope-trace">${t}</span>`;
const code = [
  `${k('int32_t')} lab_companion_app(${k('void')}* p) {`,
  `  UNUSED(p);`,
  `  ${str('// your first Flipper app, built with uFBT')}`,
  `  FURI_LOG_I(${str('"lab"')}, ${str('"hello"')});`,
  `  ${k('return')} 0;`,
  `}`,
].join('\n');
---
<Section id="method" eyebrow="How each lesson works" title="Write the prediction before you press Read." intro="Each lab asks you to write your prediction, then what the Flipper showed.">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-5">
    <article class={`${tile} flex flex-col lg:col-span-3`}>
      <div class="art" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="scope">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-x-4 font-mono text-[0.6875rem] tracking-wide text-scope-text uppercase">
            <span>Wave Lab · OOK</span><span>bits {bits.join(' ')}</span>
          </div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 480 100" class="mt-3 h-auto w-full" fill="none">
            {bits.map((b, i) => <text x={i * w + w / 2} y="98" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-scope-text font-mono text-[11px]">{b}</text>)}
            <path d="M0 60H480" stroke="var(--scope-grid)" />
            <path d={carrier} stroke="var(--scope-trace)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" />
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3 class="tile-title">See the mechanism.</h3>
      <p class="tile-body">Each mechanism comes with a figure or a tool. Wave Lab turns the bits you type into an OOK or FSK waveform. The Rolling Code Sim shows a receiver rejecting a counter it has already seen.</p>
    </article>

    <article class={`${tile} flex flex-col lg:col-span-2`}>
      <div class="art" aria-hidden="true">
        <dl class="grid gap-2 rounded-xl border border-border bg-background p-4 text-sm">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[6.5rem_1fr] gap-3">
            <dt class="text-muted-foreground">Prediction</dt>
            <dd class="font-medium">Peak near 433.92 MHz</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[6.5rem_1fr] gap-3 border-t border-dashed border-border pt-2">
            <dt class="text-muted-foreground">Observation</dt>
            <dd class="font-medium"><span class="font-mono tabular-nums">433.92</span> MHz, AM650</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[6.5rem_1fr] items-center gap-3 border-t border-dashed border-border pt-2">
            <dt class="text-muted-foreground">Check</dt>
            <dd class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-medium text-success">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"></path></svg>
              You've got it
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <h3 class="tile-title">Test your prediction.</h3>
      <p class="tile-body">You change one thing at a time and compare the result with what you wrote down. Every lab ends with a "you've got it when" check. In Module 1 the check is stating the frequency of one device you own and how you measured it. When a lab fails, Module 9's decision trees start from the symptom you saw, such as "nothing decodes".</p>
    </article>

    <article class={`${tile} flex flex-col lg:col-span-5 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.1fr)] lg:items-center lg:gap-12`}>
      <div class="art order-last mb-0 mt-7 lg:order-none lg:mt-0" aria-hidden="true">
        <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-scope-bg p-5 font-mono text-[0.8125rem] leading-relaxed text-scope-text"><code set:html={code} /></pre>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[0.6875rem] text-muted-foreground">$ ufbt launch</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="tile-title mt-0">Compile your own app.</h3>
        <p class="tile-body">In week 10 you build a small Flipper app in C with uFBT. Your notebook records the toolchain and firmware versions that built it.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-8">
    <a href="/course#lesson-shape" class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-1.5 font-medium text-primary underline decoration-primary/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary">How a lesson is laid out <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </p>
</Section>

<style>
  @reference "../../styles/global.css";
  .art {
    @apply mb-7;
  }
  .scope {
    @apply rounded-xl bg-scope-bg px-5 pt-4 pb-3;
  }
  .tile-title {
    @apply mt-auto text-xl tracking-[-0.015em];
  }
  .tile-body {
    @apply mt-2 max-w-[60ch] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground;
  }
</style>
